==English==

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|fr|machinerie||machinery}}, from {{m|fr|machine||machine}}; see {{m|en|machine}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|mə-shē'nə-rē}}, {{IPA|en|/məˈʃiːnəɹi/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-machinery.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːnəɹi}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[machine]]s constituting a production apparatus, in a plant etc., collectively.
# The working [[part]]s of a [[machine]] as a group.
# The [[collective]] parts of something which allow it to [[function]].
#: {{ux|en|All of the '''machinery''' of the law was brought to bear on the investigation.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} The literary devices used in a work, notably for dramatic effect

